    "narrative": "The priority for LawDog today is maximizing stolen base opportunities against favorable matchups, leading us to feature **Taylor Ward** (71.19) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) as our premier starts. Both benefit significantly from the plus-matchup against Fedde (xERA 5.20) and a generous wind-out condition. **Bryson Stott** (69.02) also serves as an anchor today; despite the presence of a tough opposing catcher, his platoon advantage and favorable park factors make him a high-efficiency engine for our run production. Meanwhile, **Luis Arraez** (67.68) remains a locked-in core play, with his top-of-the-order usage providing the highest projected floor of our utility options. \n\nOur most difficult personnel decision involved the benching of **Daulton Varsho** (47.91). While **Daulton Varsho** offers intriguing power-speed potential, the matchup against the sharp xERA of McLean (3.28) suppressed his efficiency score below the threshold required to crack a crowded outfield and utility rotation. We are also navigating the absence of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith**, both currently sidelined on the IL, while **Lawrence Butler** remains unavailable in today\u2019s confirmed lineup. As we chase points in a competitive 5x5 landscape, we are keeping a close watch on **Yainer Diaz** (40.38), whose low score reflects the stiff challenge posed by Ryan; should the game script turn early, we may look to pinch-hit options like **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, or **Gavin Sheets** to recover value if they become available. \n\nWe are specifically capitalizing on the slow delivery times of Pfaadt, which elevates the appeal of **Jung Hoo Lee** (64.08), **Tyler Freeman** (64.91), **Matt Chapman** (61.52), and **Drew Gilbert** (52.83). These four are positioned to aggressively exploit the base paths, as the combination of park factors and the pitcher\u2019s rhythm creates an ideal environment for our speed-oriented roster construction. While **Geraldo Perdomo** (57.43) sits in the marginal tier, his position at the top of the order remains vital for our run and stolen base metrics against Roupp. We will monitor the wind projections closely, as the potential for offensive explosions in these favorable conditions could easily turn our marginal starts into high-ceiling performances.",
